<!--
  COMPRINNO ARCHITECTURE SKELETON — 3-AZ THREE-TIER LAYOUT
  =========================================================
  Use this as the starting point for every new architecture diagram.

  HOW TO USE:
  1. Copy this file to outputs/<project-slug>/<project>.drawio.xml
  2. Replace PROJECT_NAME in both pages.
  3. Fill in the metadata (Date, Creator, Reviewer) in the title blocks.
  4. Add service icons into the labelled placeholder slots.
  5. Remove slots you don't need; add extra slots by duplicating an icon cell.
  6. Add the cluster lane(s) if compute spans AZ rows (see §14 in house-style.md).
  7. Add edges (all edges: parent="1").
  8. Fill in the Flow page.

  COORDINATE REFERENCE: .kiro/skills/arch-diagram/references/coords-cheatsheet.md
  FULL RULES:           .kiro/skills/arch-diagram/references/house-style.md

  GEOMETRY SUMMARY (do not change these container values):
    cloud:   x=260  y=250  w=2727 h=2115  (child of root)
    region:  x=247  y=285  w=2395 h=1745  (child of cloud)
    vpc:     x=85   y=260  w=2225 h=1405  (child of region)
    az1:     x=520  y=80   w=1640 h=340   (child of vpc)
    az2:     x=520  y=540  w=1640 h=340   (child of vpc)
    az3:     x=520  y=1000 w=1640 h=340   (child of vpc)
    public subnets: x=35  y=50 w=380 h=250 (child of AZ)  ← default 2-icon; scale per content
    app subnets:    x=455 y=50 w=650 h=250 (child of AZ)  ← pub_right+40
    db subnets:     x=1145 y=50 w=300 h=250 (child of AZ)  ← app_right+40, w=300 (1 icon)
    icons in subnets: w=120 h=120, y=65, x=centred
    igw: x=-60 y=650 (child of vpc)
    alb: x=160 y=650 (child of vpc)

  LANE GEOMETRY (relative to vpc, only add when compute spans AZs):
    Single lane:  x=1030 y=80 w=480 h=1260 (single lane; dual: w=240 each, gap=100px)
    Task icons:   x=180  y=110 / y=570 / y=1030  (AZ-1/2/3)
    Badge:        x=1008 y=88  w=45 h=45 (child of vpc)
-->
